# ci/asan.supp -- CONTINGENCY ONLY. Not required by measurement.
#
# Measured 2026-08-04 on pi (Ubuntu 24.04, gcc 13.3.0) with SPOOLES itself compiled
# -fsanitize=address,undefined (952 __asan_report_* references in libspooles.a), over
# example1 + control1/hinf1/truss5/truss6/truss8 + the three malformed inputs, AND
# additionally with the sparse path forced on (sdpa_chordal.cpp "#if 0 // SPARSE
# computation for debugging" flipped to #if 1, so Chordal::Spooles_MMD / _ND / _MS all
# execute): 0 AddressSanitizer reports, 0 LeakSanitizer reports, 0 UBSan reports.
#
# So SPOOLES is NOT noisy and this file should stay unused. Enable it only if a
# different runner image produces third-party reports, and delete entries again once
# they stop appearing -- a live suppression here can hide a first-party regression,
# because interceptor_via_lib matches the whole archive.
#
# interceptor_via_fun:IVL_*
# interceptor_via_fun:Graph_*
# interceptor_via_fun:ETree_*
# interceptor_via_fun:InpMtx_*
